        "r": 150.5854,
        "b": 533.4880469606776
      },
      "content": "Control Operation",
      "level": 2,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "section_heading",
      "semantic_role": "section_heading",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0176",
      "reading_order": 180,
      "section": "Control Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.564299999999974,
        "t": 521.9326068359375,
        "r": 291.37819999999994,
        "b": 499.3747492035387
      },
      "content": "To understand control operation, refer to the following text and the schematic diagram (Figure 3-3).",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0177",
      "reading_order": 181,
      "section": "Control Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.564299999999974,
        "t": 486.5566068359375,
        "r": 291.56850000000026,
        "b": 426.0146492035388
      },
      "content": "Starting Sequence: When start/stop switch S11 is held in the Stop (preheat) position, battery B+ is connected to the coil of heater relay K13.  The relay contacts close and connect B+ to heaters HR1 HR4.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0178",
      "reading_order": 182,
      "section": "Control Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.564299999999974,
        "t": 413.19650683593756,
        "r": 291.44639999999987,
        "b": 327.42714920353893
      },
      "content": "After the preheat time interval, the operator holds S11 in the Start position.  This connects B+ to K14 fuel solenoid relay and through A11-K15 NC (normally closed) contacts to K11 start solenoid relay. These relays actuate K1 fuel solenoid, B1 solenoid/ starter motor and heaters HR1 - HR4 (via K13 NC contacts).",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0179",
      "reading_order": 183,
      "section": "Control Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.564299999999974,
        "t": 314.6090068359377,
        "r": 291.4640000000001,
        "b": 228.839649203539
      },
      "content": "A11-K12 power relay is actuated after a short delay, when the control power latch switch S6 closes.  S6 is closed when oil pressure rises to 5 psi (34 kPa), assuring engine lubrication before the set reaches full operating speed.  Normally open (NO) contacts on A11-K12 close, supplying B+ to the other components on the engine monitor board.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0180",
      "reading_order": 184,
      "section": "Control Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9374,
        "t": 737.9935068359378,
        "r": 564.9415999999983,
        "b": 626.9395492035392
      },
      "content": "Start-Disconnect  Sequence: As  the  generator gains speed and output voltage, A11-K15 starter protection relay energizes at  about  90  VAC. A11-K15 NC contact opens and de-energizes start solenoid relay K11.  K11 then disconnects B+ from the starter solenoid (to stop the cranking motor) and from the glow plug heaters.  If the generator fails to develop voltage, the engine will attempt to start but will stop as soon as the Start switch is released.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0181",
      "reading_order": 185,
      "section": "Control Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9374,
        "t": 610.7763068359379,
        "r": 564.7567999999994,
        "b": 588.2184492035392
      },
      "content": "The two K15 NO (normally open) contacts close and function as follows:",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0182",
      "reading_order": 186,
      "section": "Control Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 330.7465,
        "t": 572.4779068359375,
        "r": 564.7539999999996,
        "b": 536.9057492035388
      },
      "content": " Closes circuit for S1 and S2 (low oil pressure and high coolant temperature switches respectively)",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0183",
      "reading_order": 187,
      "section": "Control Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 330.7465,
        "t": 521.1141068359375,
        "r": 564.7451999999995,
        "b": 498.1842492035388
      },
      "content": " Provides  another  ground  path  for  K12  coil (through K11 coil) similar to S6.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0184",
      "reading_order": 188,
      "section": "Control Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.93899999999996,
        "t": 482.0782068359376,
        "r": 564.7649999999999,
        "b": 434.17854920353886
      },
      "content": "Battery Charge Circuit: Alternator G1, powered by a belt from the engine, supplies B+ voltage to recharge the generator set starting battery through circuit breaker CB13.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0185",
      "reading_order": 189,
      "section": "Control Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.93899999999996,
        "t": 418.07250683593765,
        "r": 565.0378,
        "b": 344.945449203539
      },
      "content": "Stopping Sequence: Placing S11 in the Stop position puts B+ (through diode CR2) on the ground side of the A11-K12 power relay.  This causes K12 to deenergize and disconnect B+ from CB12 and K1 fuel solenoid.  De-energizing K1 shuts off the fuel flow to stop the engine.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0186",
      "reading_order": 190,
      "section": "Control Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.93899999999996,
        "t": 328.78220683593776,
        "r": 564.7682999999994,
        "b": 280.93974920353907
      },
      "content": "Fault  Shutdown: Fault  breaker  CB12  opens  to stop the engine any time a fault sensor closes the circuit to ground.  The fault sensors as shown in Figure 3-2 are:",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_179",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_179",
          "title": "Control Operation"
        }
      ],
      "page": 14,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
